course: dictionary
lesson: 4454
title: Happen: what takes place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To happen means to take place, or to come about. When you ask «What happened?», you want to know what took place.
explain: To happen to someone means that person is the one who goes through it. «Something funny happened to me» means something came about, and I was the one it came to.
explain: To happen to do something means to do it by chance, not on purpose. «I happened to see her» means I saw her by luck. If someone planned it, you would say «I planned to see her».
fact: Happen is a verb: happen, happens, happened, happening.
fact: «Happened» is the past tense: it tells us something already took place.
fact: «Happens» is used for things that take place regularly or are happening now: «Most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor.»
fact: «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why, so that it never happens again.»
fact: «Befell» is an old word that means happened: «Animals all, as it befell.»
exercise: «The kind words protect feelings, but you still need to know what really happened.» What does happened mean here? | A loud noise | A wrong answer | *The things that took place | A happy party
exercise: Nadia says, «Something funny happened to me on the bus.» What does happened to me mean? | *Something took place, and I was the one who went through it | I made it happen on purpose | I was on the bus by chance | Someone else did the funny thing
exercise: «I happened to see her at the shop.» What does happened to see mean? | *I saw her by chance | I saw her on purpose, after a plan | I did not see her at all | I saw her only in a photo
test: «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders help investigators find out why, so that it never happens again.» What does happens mean here? | It is written down | *It takes place, it comes about | It gets better | It is a secret
test: «Animals all, as it befell.» What does befell mean? | *happened | flew | hid | asked
exam: Which sentence uses happen to mean do something by chance? | *I happened to meet my cousin at the park | I want to meet my cousin at the park | My cousin meets me every day | We will plan a meeting with my cousin
